<p class="center-text">
  There are four levels available. Here is a short description of each:
</p>

<div class="grid-columns">
  <div class="grid-item">
    <div class="heading-and-icon">
      <%= icon('gear') %>
      <h3>Admins</h3>
    </div>

    <p>
      One or two people responsible for the initial app setup and user
      management. They have the same abilities as
      <strong>Reviewers</strong>, but they can also
      edit/remove other people's issues, tasks, comments, etc.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid-item">
    <div class="heading-and-icon">
      <%= icon('ribbon') %>
      <h3>Reviewers</h3>
    </div>

    <p>
      Basically, the project managers. They can do some app setup like create
      Categories and Projects. However, their main responsibility is managing
      issues and tasks.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid-item">
    <div class="heading-and-icon">
      <%= icon('settings') %>
      <h3>Workers</h3>
    </div>

    <p>
      The busy bees working on tasks. In addition, they can report issues and
      self-assign tasks.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid-item">
    <div class="heading-and-icon">
      <%= icon('speakerphone') %>
      <h3>Reporters</h3>
    </div>

    <p>
      Everyone else can open issues, add comments, and see activity.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<hr>

<div class="heading-and-icon">
  <%= icon("person-add") %>
  <h3>Sign Up Options</h3>
</div>

<div class="grid-columns">
  <dl>
    <dt>Closed</dt>
    <dd>
      Invitation only by a Reviewer or Admin. User will receive an email which provides
      them with a link to add a password.
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <dl>
    <dt>Open</dt>
    <dd>
      Anyone with a working email address can add themselves as a Reporter.
      To protect privacy, email addresses are obfuscated. Invitations are also possible.
    </dd>
  </dl>
</div>
